  {
   "id": "wifTM73xuvcJ",
   "from": "Felix Schönbrodt",
   "author": "3f3060000990daa6",
   "date": "2012-11-26T11:44:18Z",
   "subject": "fixed.x=FALSE or TRUE in multiple regression?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi all,<br><br>I run several multiple regressions with lavaan, where some models are nested by putting constraints on the paths. I need the intercepts, so I set <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">meanstructure</span> to TRUE. Now I am not sure about the <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">fixed.x</span> option. I read the help page for it, but I am not sure what would be the correct way of doing it.<br><br>When no constraints are present, results are identical (fixed.x = TRUE or FALSE), but as soon as one path is constrained to be 0, or other equality constraints are set, results can diverge a lot.<br><br>Can someone clarify this option, or direct me to a paper where I can read about the difference? What would be the correct option for plain multiple regressions (1 DV, with constraints)?<br><br>Here&#39;s a minimal example:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lavaan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">set</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0xBEEF</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>z </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>m1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;z ~ b1*x + b2*y&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>m2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;z ~ b1*x + 0*y&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>m3 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;z ~ b1*x + b2*y<br>b1==b2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>s1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> meanstructure</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>s2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> meanstructure</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">fixed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># m1 gives identical results for s1 and s2, m2 and m3 gives different results</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br><br><br>Thanks,<br>Felix<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "yoJ7ulBnojIJ",
   "from": "yrosseel",
   "author": "89c9fc822e34b78c",
   "date": "2012-11-26T19:31:42Z",
   "subject": "Re: fixed.x=FALSE or TRUE in multiple regression?",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "&gt; I run several multiple regressions with lavaan, where some models are\r<br>&gt; nested by putting constraints on the paths. I need the intercepts, so I\r<br>&gt; set meanstructure to TRUE. Now I am not sure about the fixed.x option. I\r<br>&gt; read the help page for it, but I am not sure what would be the correct\r<br>&gt; way of doing it.\r<br>\r<br>&gt; When no constraints are present, results are identical (fixed.x = TRUE\r<br>&gt; or FALSE), but as soon as one path is constrained to be 0, or other\r<br>&gt; equality constraints are set, results can diverge a lot.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "If the results diverge, is is most likely a bug. But the dev version has \r<br>fixed many issues in this area (the special case of univariate \r<br>regression). Could you try again with dev version?\r<br>\r<br>fixed.x=TRUE or FALSE should have NO effect on the final parameter \r<br>estimates.\r<br>\r<br>For regression models, fixed.X=TRUE is the more natural choice.\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ylIL5yZRBxsJ",
   "from": "Felix Schönbrodt",
   "author": "3f3060000990daa6",
   "date": "2012-12-03T19:46:12Z",
   "subject": "Re: fixed.x=FALSE or TRUE in multiple regression?",
   "parts": [
    [
     3,
     "<blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\" class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\" class=\"gmail_quote\">I run several multiple regressions with lavaan, where some models are<br>nested by putting constraints on the paths. I need the intercepts, so I<br>set meanstructure to TRUE. Now I am not sure about the fixed.x option. I<br>read the help page for it, but I am not sure what would be the correct<br>way of doing it.<br><br>When no constraints are present, results are identical (fixed.x = TRUE<br>or FALSE), but as soon as one path is constrained to be 0, or other<br>equality constraints are set, results can diverge a lot.<br></blockquote></blockquote><br><blockquote><div style=\"text-align:left\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\" class=\"gmail_quote\">If the results diverge, is is most likely a bug. But the dev version has fixed many issues in this area (the special case of univariate regression). Could you try again with dev version?<br><br>fixed.x=TRUE or FALSE should have NO effect on the final parameter estimates.<br></blockquote></div></blockquote><br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "With the dev version parameter estimates still diverge in some cases, as soon as a parameter constraint is present (see example below).<br>Interestingly, s3a, s3b, and s2b give identical results; model s2a throws an error and has different parameter estimates:<br><br>s2a &lt;- sem(m2, data=df, meanstructure=TRUE)<br>Warning message:<br>In x[lavaanParTable$unco[lavaanParTable$op == &quot;~&quot; &amp; lavaanParTable$unco]] &lt;- x.beta[-1L] :<br>number of items to replace is not a multiple of replacement length<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">### minimal example #######</span></div></code></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lavaan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">set</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0xBEEF</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>z </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>m2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;</span></div></code></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#080\"><br>z ~ b1*x + 0*y<br>&quot;</span></div></code></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#080\"></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>m3 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;</span></div></code></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#080\"><br>z ~ b1*x + b2*y<br></span></div></code></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#080\">b2==0<br>&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># m2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>s2a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> meanstructure</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s2a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>s2b </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> meanstructure</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">fixed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s2b</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># m3</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>s3a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> meanstructure</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s3a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>s3b </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> meanstructure</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">fixed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s3b</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#################</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>sessionInfo</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>R version </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.15</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</s